INT. LAUNDROMAT - DAY

Rows of humming dryers. Fluorescent lights. A television bolted high on the wall plays a cooking show with the sound off.

PERPETUA DUNMORE (50s, bright cardigan, folding towels with military precision) works at a table. Nearby, her nephew BARTHOLOMEW "BART" CASSIDY (20s, wrinkled hoodie, guitar case) sits on a dryer, scrolling his phone. At the vending machine, a stranger, IMOGEN FAIRBANKS (30s, crisp suit, rolling suitcase), feeds coins into the slot.

PERPETUA
Bart, get off the dryer.

BART
It's off.

PERPETUA
The principle is on.

IMOGEN
(to the machine)
Come on, come on.

The machine rattles. A bag of pretzels hangs from the spiral, refusing to drop.

BART
You have to shake it.

IMOGEN
I'm not shaking a vending machine.

PERPETUA
Everyone shakes the vending machine.

IMOGEN
I have a flight in two hours.

BART
Then shake it faster.

Imogen glares, then grips the machine and rocks it. The pretzels fall. She straightens her blazer with great dignity.

PERPETUA
^Nicely done.

BART
^Nicely done.

They say it at the same time and look at each other, startled. Imogen fights a smile.

A voice crackles from the ceiling speaker.

MANAGER (V.O.)
(over intercom)
Attention customers. Machine seven is on fire. Machine seven is on fire. This is not a drill.

Everyone turns. Machine seven is, in fact, on fire. A thin orange flame licks the lint trap.

PERPETUA
Of course it is.

BART
Water?

IMOGEN
(heading for the door)
I'm not paid for this.

BART
Nobody is!

Perpetua drags a bucket across the floor and dumps it in. The fire dies with a sad hiss. A single towel drifts out, charred and smoking.

IMOGEN
(from the doorway)
Is this a regular occurrence?

PERPETUA
Tuesdays.

Imogen laughs despite herself, tears open her pretzels, and offers one to Bart.
